====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[kick]]s.
# {{lb|en|sports}} One who takes kicks.
## {{lb|en|American football}} A [[placekicker]]: a [[player]] who kicks the football during [[free kick]]s, [[kick off]]s, [[field goal]]s, and [[extra point]] tries.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The [[kicking strap]].
# {{lb|en|nautical|informal}} An [[outboard motor]].
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} An unexpected [[situation]], [[detail]] or circumstance, often [[unpleasant]], serving as a [[punchline]] or [[clincher]].
#: {{ux|en|John wants to climb the wall, but the '''kicker''' is that it is thirty feet tall.}}
#: {{ux|en|Tuition is free; the '''kicker''' is that mandatory room and board costs twice as much as at other colleges.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=David Zelman|title=If I Can, You Can: Transformation Made Easy
|passage=If the coffee is currently being spilled, I can't unspill it. And here's the '''kicker'''. You can't change the future, because it hasn't happened yet.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|artist=Drake|title=Gyalchester|album=More Life|year=2017|passage=They want me gone, wait for the '''kicker''' / Bury me now and I only get bigger}}
# {{lb|en|finance}} An enticement for investors, e.g. [[warranty]] added to the investment contract.
# {{lb|en|poker}} An [[unpaired]] [[card]] which is part of a [[pair]], [[two pair]], or [[three of a kind]] poker hand.
#: {{ux|en|Jill's hand was two pair, aces and sevens, with a king '''kicker'''.}}
# {{lb|en|journalism}} Small text above a [[headline]] that indicates the topic of the story.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1981|author=Harry W. Stonecipher|author2=Edward C. Nicholls|author3=Douglas A. Anderson|title=Electronic Age News Editing|page=104
|passage=[[hammer|Hammers]] are, in essence, reverse '''kickers'''. Instead of being set in smaller type like '''kickers''', hammers are set in larger type than headlines.}}
# {{lb|en|journalism}} The last one or two paragraphs of a story.
# {{lb|en|journalism}} {{synonym of|en|lead-in|gloss=start of photo caption}}
# {{lb|en|radio|television}} A [[lighthearted]] or [[humorous]] item used to [[round off]] a [[news]] [[broadcast]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1984|title=Media Report to Women|volume=12|page=46
|passage={{...}} international news and politics, and heavy on the light stuff: local news, entertainment and merry little '''kickers''' {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Frank Barnas|author2=Ted White|title=Broadcast News Writing, Reporting, and Producing|page=77
|passage=Instead, a reporter can carve out a niche as an entertainment/community reporter, thus concentrating their efforts on filing feature stories for the E block, where the '''''kickers''''' are slated. '''Kickers''' are feel-good pieces placed at the end of the newscast to leave viewers in a good mood {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|printing}} A [[device]] that periodically [[displace]]s a [[newspaper]] from the print production line, to aid in gathering the newspapers into fixed-size [[bundle]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1931|title=Official Gazette of the United States Patent Office|page=490
|passage=In a printing machine, the combination of a '''kicker''' mechanism for displacing a newspaper {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[launch ramp]].
# {{lb|en|prison slang}} The fermenting mass of fruit that is the basis of [[pruno]], or "prison wine".
#: {{synonyms|en|motor}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A relaxed party.
#: {{syn|en|kickback}}
# {{lb|en|film|television}} A [[backlight]] positioned at an angle.
#: {{synonyms|en|kick}}
# {{lb|en|pinball}} A rubber pad that propels the ball away upon impact, like a [[bumper]], but usually a horizontal side of a wall.
# {{lb|en|performance art}} A practitioner of the [[kicking]] performance art.
# {{lb|en|US|slang|archaic}} A [[complainer]].

